@startuml
' Figure - Composite Structure Diagram: internals of the integrity verifier
!include _header.txt

interface "EvidenceItem" as pIn
interface "IntegrityReport" as pOut

package "GraphIntegrityEngine" <<composite>> {
  component "dagBuilder : DagBuilder"          as DB
  component "walker : DepthFirstWalker"        as W
  component "hashCheck : ContentCheck"         as C1
  component "sigCheck : AuthorshipCheck"       as C2
  component "timeCheck : OrderCheck"           as C3
  component "collector : FailureCollector"     as FC
  component "scorer : CompletenessScorer"      as CS
}

pIn --> DB  : evidence
DB  --> W   : rooted node list
W   --> C1  : node
W   --> C2  : node
W   --> C3  : node, predecessor time
C1  --> FC  : NodeFailure
C2  --> FC  : NodeFailure
C3  --> FC  : NodeFailure
W   --> FC  : verified count
FC  --> CS
CS  --> pOut : verdict, completeness, failures

note right of FC
  The collector sits BETWEEN the checks and the
  scorer, and nothing routes a failure back to
  the walker. That absent connector is the
  structural reason a failure does not stop the
  traversal - the property SR-26 requires.
end note
@enduml
